    "title": "Will Mets end losing streak today vs Dodgers? How to watch, prediction",
    "text": "April 14, 2026, 11:35 a.m. ETThe New York Mets look to finally put an end to their losing streak as they get ready for another contest against the Los Angeles Dodgers on Tuesday night.The Mets (7-10, last in NL East) were shutout for a second straight game in a 4-0 series opening loss on Monday. The scoreless drought has now hit 20 innings for the Mets, who last scored a run in the seventh inning in the series finale versus the Athletics on Saturday, April 11.The Dodgers (12-4, first in NL West) scored four runs early against Mets starter David Peterson, as Andy Pages hit a three-run home run in the bottom of the third inning to put L.A. up for good. Starting pitcher Justin Wrobleski had his best career start, as the 25-year-old southpaw pitched eight shutout innings and only allowed two hits and no walks for his second win of the season.The Mets have now lost six consecutive games, their longest losing streak since late in last year's regular season when the team dropped a season-high eight games in a row in early September to eliminate any chance of making the playoffs.Will the Mets put an end to the losing streak tonight?Here's how to watch, the starting pitching matchup and our prediction for tonight's Mets vs. Dodgers game.:What time is NY Mets vs Dodgers game today?Time: 10:10 p.m. ETWhat channel is NY Mets vs Dodgers today?TV: SNYHow to stream NY Mets vs Dodgers game todayStreaming: MLB.TV for out of market viewersNY Mets, Dodgers starting pitchers todayMets: Nolan McLean (1-1, 2.70 ERA)Dodgers: Yoshinobu Yamamoto (2-1, 2.50 ERA)McLean has continued his solid start to 2026, as the 24-year-old right-hander has allowed two or fewer runs in all three starts so far this season in 16 2/3 innings. In his most recent appearance, McLean pitched a season-long 6 1/3 innings and tied a season-high with eight strikeouts, but was given his first loss of the year as the Mets offense couldn't generate much at all in a 7-1 loss to the Arizona Diamondbacks on April 9.Yamamoto, the reigning World Series MVP, high strikeout numbers have yet to be there but the 27-year-old Japanese ace continues to shine, as he pitched six innings for a third consecutive outing and surrendered just one run on five hits in the Dodgers' 4-1 victory over the Toronto Blue Jays in the World Series rematch on April 7.NY Mets vs Dodgers odds for today's gameOdds according to BetMGM as of Tuesday, April 14:Spread: Dodgers by 1.5Over/under: 7.5Moneyline: Dodgers (-200), Mets (+165)Prediction for Mets vs Dodgers todayThe Mets offense finally breaks the scoreless streak early in this one, but it's still not enough.McLean has his worst start yet, giving up three or more runs for the first time this season as the Dodgers offense takes advantage of the young pitcher and win the series as the Mets losing streak hits seven games.Dodgers 7, Mets 4",
